- ## cataclysm
+ ## cataclysm

- - The givens `cataclysm.Css.Convertible.srgb: Srgb is Css.Convertible of "color"` and
-   `Css.Convertible.chroma: Chroma is Css.Convertible of "color"` replaced by one
-   `Css.Convertible.chromatic: [color] => ((? >: color) is Chromatic) => color is Css.Convertible of
-   "color"`, which renders any colour with a `Chromatic` instance for it or a supertype (every iridescence colour form, through
-   `Color.chromatic`, and `Chroma` itself) as a `#00ff88`-style triplet. `Srgb` values render identically.
-   `cataclysm.core` depends on `anticipation.color` and no longer on `iridescence.core`; a consumer
-   that reached iridescence only through cataclysm must declare it. (#2082)
- - `cataclysm.core` no longer ships or reads the classpath resources `/cataclysm/properties.json`
-   and `/cataclysm/syntaxes.json`: the MDN property and syntax tables are compiled into string
-   tables (`cataclysm.CssData`, private) at build time from `lib/cataclysm/data`. Behaviour of
-   `PropertyDef` and `SyntaxMatcher` is unchanged. `cataclysm.core` no longer depends on
-   `jacinta.core` or `hellenism.core` and is no longer marked JVM/JS-only; `cataclysm.html` (which
-   reads stylesheets with `cp"…"`) declares `hellenism.core` itself. A consumer that reached jacinta
-   or hellenism only through `cataclysm.core` must declare it. (#2082)
- - New module `cataclysm.fonts` (in the `web` bundle; dependencies `cataclysm.core`, `phoenicia.core`,
-   `monotonous.core`, `anticipation.url`) now holds the font half of cataclysm: `cataclysm.Web` (with
-   its generic-family `Typesettable` givens), `cataclysm.FontFace`, the `style` extensions on
-   `phoenicia.Face` and `Font`, and `Css.fontFace(font)`/`Css.fontFaces(fonts*)`, which are now
-   extensions on `Css.type` defined in that module rather than methods of `object Css` (call sites
-   are unchanged given `import cataclysm.*` or `import soundness.*`). Package and names are
-   unchanged; the `soundness` exports of `Web`, `FontFace` and `style` moved to
-   `soundness_cataclysm_fonts`. `cataclysm.core` no longer depends on `phoenicia.core`,
-   `monotonous.core` or `anticipation.url`; a consumer using any of these, or the fonts API, through
-   `cataclysm.core` must declare `cataclysm.fonts` (savagery and tasseomancy now do). (#2082)
+ - Los givens `cataclysm.Css.Convertible.srgb: Srgb is Css.Convertible of "color"` y
+   `Css.Convertible.chroma: Chroma is Css.Convertible of "color"` se sustituyen por un único
+   `Css.Convertible.chromatic: [color] => ((? >: color) is Chromatic) => color is Css.Convertible of "color"`,
+   que representa cualquier color que tenga una instancia de `Chromatic` para él o para un supertipo
+   (todas las formas de color de iridescence, mediante `Color.chromatic`, y el propio `Chroma`) como
+   un triplete al estilo de `#00ff88`. Los valores `Srgb` se representan de forma idéntica.
+   `cataclysm.core` depende de `anticipation.color` y ya no de `iridescence.core`; un consumidor que
+   llegaba a iridescence solo a través de cataclysm debe declararlo. (#2082)
+ - `cataclysm.core` ya no incluye ni lee los recursos del classpath `/cataclysm/properties.json` y
+   `/cataclysm/syntaxes.json`: las tablas de propiedades y de sintaxis de MDN se compilan en tablas
+   de cadenas (`cataclysm.CssData`, privada) en tiempo de construcción a partir de
+   `lib/cataclysm/data`. El comportamiento de `PropertyDef` y `SyntaxMatcher` no cambia.
+   `cataclysm.core` ya no depende de `jacinta.core` ni de `hellenism.core` y ya no está marcado como
+   exclusivo de JVM/JS; `cataclysm.html` (que lee hojas de estilo con `cp"…"`) declara él mismo
+   `hellenism.core`. Un consumidor que llegaba a jacinta o a hellenism solo a través de
+   `cataclysm.core` debe declararlo. (#2082)
+ - El nuevo módulo `cataclysm.fonts` (en la agrupación `web`; dependencias `cataclysm.core`,
+   `phoenicia.core`, `monotonous.core`, `anticipation.url`) contiene ahora la mitad tipográfica de
+   cataclysm: `cataclysm.Web` (con sus givens `Typesettable` de familias genéricas),
+   `cataclysm.FontFace`, las extensiones `style` sobre `phoenicia.Face` y `Font`, y
+   `Css.fontFace(font)`/`Css.fontFaces(fonts*)`, que ahora son extensiones sobre `Css.type` definidas
+   en ese módulo en lugar de métodos de `object Css` (los puntos de llamada no cambian con
+   `import cataclysm.*` o `import soundness.*`). El paquete y los nombres no cambian; las
+   exportaciones de `soundness` de `Web`, `FontFace` y `style` se trasladan a
+   `soundness_cataclysm_fonts`. `cataclysm.core` ya no depende de `phoenicia.core`, `monotonous.core`
+   ni `anticipation.url`; un consumidor que use cualquiera de ellos, o la API de fuentes, a través de
+   `cataclysm.core` debe declarar `cataclysm.fonts` (savagery y tasseomancy ya lo hacen). (#2082)

- ## bitumen
+ ## bitumen

- - `bitumen.Tar.Body` (the class, `Tar.Body.apply(chunks: Data*)` and `Tar.Body.empty`) renamed
